@startuml
title Anonymous pipe shared through fork(): the child writes, the parent reads
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  ParticipantBorderColor #2E8B67
  LifeLineBorderColor #2E8B67
  ArrowColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
participant "Parent" as p
participant "Kernel\n(pipe object)" as k
participant "Child" as c

p -> k : pipe(pipe_fd)
k --> p : pipe_fd[0] = read end\npipe_fd[1] = write end
p -> k : fork()
k --> c : child starts with copies\nof both descriptors
note over p, c
  After fork(), both processes hold both ends.
  Each closes the end it does not use.
end note
c -> k : close(pipe_fd[0])
p -> k : close(pipe_fd[1])
p -> k : read(pipe_fd[0], buffer, 80)
note right of p : blocks: the pipe is empty
c -> k : write(pipe_fd[1], "Hello, I am your child\\n", 24)
k --> p : read() returns 24 bytes
p -> p : printf("I got from the child: %s", buffer)
c -> k : close(pipe_fd[1])
c -> k : exit(0)
p -> k : close(pipe_fd[0])
p -> k : waitpid(pid, NULL, 0)
k --> p : child reaped
@enduml
